WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:11.260
28. The Pygmalion Effect. You get what you expect. That's the Pygmalion

2
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:18.580
effect in a nutshell. Studies show that people tend to live up to, or down to, the expectations

3
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:24.120
people place on them. Our reality really is influenced by the opinions

4
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:30.200
and expectations of others. When other people expect us to be great, we are more likely

5
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:36.300
to be great. When we aren't expected to perform well, we usually won't bother. It

6
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:42.840
is amazing how affected we are by the labels people attach to us. Many studies have demonstrated

7
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:49.620
the Pygmalion effect. One study, by Robert Rosenthal and Lenore Jacobson, randomly selected

8
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:56.140
students in several classrooms. Teachers were told that these students were especially smart.

9
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:02.020
The teachers, therefore, expected high performance from these students, and they got it. At the

10
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.740
end of the year, the randomly selected students had increased their IQs and performed better

11
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:13.220
overall than the rest, even though they were actually no better or smarter than the rest

12
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:18.580
of the class. Their teachers had believed that they had great potential, and that had

13
00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.840
caused the potential to appear. There is a downside to the Pygmalion Effect,

14
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:31.280
of course. Just as we rise to meet high expectations, we may be knocked down by low expectations.

15
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:37.320
Jane Elliott conducted a famous test on school children. She divided them by eye color, blue

16
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:43.160
versus brown. One day, the blue-eyed group was praised, while those with brown eyes were

17
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:48.800
told they were inferior. The next day, the roles were reversed. Students took spelling

18
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:55.340
tests on both days. Most students did very badly on the day they were made to feel inferior.

19
00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:03.000
Labels can create reality. People who are expected to fail often fail. People who are

20
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:09.640
labeled as winners generally win. If you want to get the best from yourself, expect it.
